Give PW Docs its own AppUserModelID.

extras/projicons/ProjIcons.pro declares APP_USER_MODEL_ID a second time,
separately from desktop-apps/win-linux/src/defines.h. defines.h was rebranded
to PW.Docs.1; this one was left at the upstream ASC.Documents.5, and it is the
value the projicons subproject actually compiles. Windows groups taskbar
buttons and jumplists by that id, so PW Docs shared a taskbar entry with any
other app still carrying it.

Apply to: desktop-apps/win-linux/extras/projicons/ProjIcons.pro

--- a/desktop-apps/win-linux/extras/projicons/ProjIcons.pro
+++ b/desktop-apps/win-linux/extras/projicons/ProjIcons.pro
@@ -4,5 +4,5 @@
 DEFINES += APP_ICON_PATH=\"./res/icons/pwdocs.ico\"
-DEFINES += APP_USER_MODEL_ID=\\\"ASC.Documents.5\\\"
+DEFINES += APP_USER_MODEL_ID=\\\"PW.Docs.1\\\"
 DEFINES += COPYRIGHT_YEAR=$${CURRENT_YEAR}
